  "reasoning": "The defendant repeatedly snatched personal belongings (a bag with a phone, cash, ID, and gold necklaces) from victims who were unprepared, without any indication of violence or threats beyond the act of snatching. Under Chinese Criminal Law, such conduct constitutes the offense of 抢夺罪 (robbery by snatching), which is distinct from ordinary theft (盗窃罪) and robbery (抢劫罪). The facts explicitly support a charge of 抢夺, and no other separate crimes are indicated.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]抢夺<eoa>"
